      "max_rel_diff": 2.3857098964052823e-09,
      "identical": true,
      "meaning": "At h=1 the TFIM is self-dual with Z_jZ_{j+1} <-> X_j, so the T and X arms are the SAME continuum operator (energy density, Delta=1). HYP-2026-008's registered test therefore compared epsilon against epsilon and could not discriminate. The true spin primary is Z_j (Delta=1/8), measured here as the Z arm."
    },
    "preregistration_deviation": {
      "registered": "three arms (eps, T, X); primary contrast T vs X",
      "executed": "four arms (eps, T, X, Z); primary contrast T vs Z",
      "reason": "The Kramers-Wannier self-duality identity verified in this same run shows T and X are the same continuum operator at h=1, making the registered contrast vacuous. Z (the true spin primary) was added to supply a real one.",
